## .claude / .agents external-skill leak: SKIPPED
creating a '.claude/' path is gated by this worktree's harness hook; per the lead this sub-test is
recorded and skipped, not worked around. From opencode's own built-in config reference (dumped by
'opencode debug skill' in compat.log): external skills AUTO-LOAD from ~/.claude/skills and
~/.agents/skills (HOME-anchored), toggled off by OPENCODE_DISABLE_CLAUDE_CODE_SKILLS=1 /
OPENCODE_DISABLE_EXTERNAL_SKILLS=1. So with HOME = the user's own home, those DO leak unless the
daemon sets those env vars or points HOME at a dedicated soma home.
## findings
~/.config/opencode username sentinel in A (XDG redirected)=0, in B (XDG default to $HOME/.config)=1
~/.config/opencode/agent sentinel in A=0, in B=3
~/.opencode/agent (HOME-anchored) seen anywhere=13 (config reference says ~/.opencode is NOT a config/agent source)
VERDICT: PASS — redirecting XDG_CONFIG_HOME fully isolates opencode's global config (the fake ~/.config/opencode sentinel is invisible in A), but with no XDG redirect it defaults to $HOME/.config and the user's ~/.config/opencode LEAKS (visible in B). A soma daemon must redirect XDG_CONFIG_HOME (or point HOME at a dedicated soma home); ~/.claude|~/.agents skills leak too (documented, hook-skipped).
